ittle bit  about how you how that worked how you  got into that  well so the situation was that that um  nobody really understood what was there  it was sort of a state secret  the oil industry was a state secret um  uh  you know all these big companies were  not known  um to the russians and the russians had  these these uh  vouchers they called them privatization  certificates and they could  invest their vouchers and whatever they  wanted to invest them in or sell their  vouchers  and most russians didn't really think  that their vouchers would be worth  anything and so they sold them for a  bottle of vodka and  and various people were were buying up  vouchers and this voucher exchange  exchanges formed and and i did the math  and  and i said okay if you buy shares and  some of these oil companies you're  buying  oil had like 10 cents per barrel of oil  reserves in the ground and at the time  oil prices were let's say trading at 30  and so 10 cents on the ground versus 30  out of the ground that that kind of had  to be a good deal  and so um but but to tell you the truth  it was  it was really hard to get people  interested in the west in that i would  say look here you know these things are  trading at a 99.9  discount and most people when they heard  the word russia they  like ran for the hills and so it wasn't  like um this was something  that was like the slam dunk you know  obvious  to most people most people said well you  know whatever the valuations are  i don't want to go anywhere near russia  so ultimately  um you fell out of favor in russia  um and ultimately were even  expelled from the country legal problems  what what went wrong how did the problem  start to develop  well so the companies that i so i ended  up getting becoming the largest  foreign investor in russia we had four  and a half billion dollars  invested in all these companies and what  i discovered was all the companies were  basically being robbed blind  by these oligarchs who were the 